  "scenario": "With stock Plasma and EQOS IRQ on CPU6, repeat one 8-second, 300 Mbit/s IPv4 UDP receive flow in A/B/B/A order using default socket buffers. Run one matched A/B pair with larger test sockets. Separately run one 12-second IPv4 TCP stream in each direction per A/B/A phase. A is the control and B enables RIWT 64, TX IOC interval 8, and ordinary IPv4 checksum flags. Take local CPU snapshots around each TCP flow.",
  "expected": "Compare UDP loss against target socket counters. Test whether the combined profile preserves TCP throughput and reduces board CPU per received gigabit.",
  "observed": "At 41600 bytes of actual receive buffer, UDP loss was 979/879/851/1265 datagrams in A/B/B/A order. The target full-socket counters matched every loss count. With verified 131072-byte test sockets at both ends, A and B had zero loss. TCP throughput was 937.588–941.144 Mbit/s with no retransmissions. Combined TCP RX used less busy CPU and interrupt CPU per delivered gigabit than both controls. Combined TCP TX busy CPU fell within the control range.",
  "duration_seconds": null,
